00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,075
Store sixty five in i, and i reads sixty five.

2
00:00:04,075 --> 00:00:12,890
Store three point one four in f, and now i reads a huge meaningless number: the float's bits read as an integer.

3
00:00:12,890 --> 00:00:15,716
Writing one member destroys the others.

4
00:00:15,716 --> 00:00:19,934
Unions save memory when you need only one field at a time.

